From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH BlueZ 1/2] adapter: Fix crash on zero-length start discovery reply

start_discovery_complete() validates the reply length before using the
returned parameters:

	if (length < sizeof(*rp)) {
		btd_error(adapter->dev_id,
			"Wrong size of start discovery return parameters");
		discovery_complete(adapter, MGMT_STATUS_FAILED);
		return;
	}

but that check sits *below* the branch taken when the discovery client
list has emptied while the command was pending, and that branch has
already dereferenced the reply:

	if (!adapter->discovery_list) {
		struct mgmt_cp_stop_discovery cp;

		if (status != MGMT_STATUS_SUCCESS)
			return;

		/* Stop discovering as there are no clients left */
		cp.type = rp->type;      <-- rp may be NULL here

mgmt_cp_start_discovery is a single uint8_t, so rp->type is a one-byte
read at offset 0 and a NULL rp faults immediately.

param is NULL whenever the request completes without parameters. In
src/shared/mgmt.c a Command Status event dispatches

	request_complete(mgmt, cs->status, opcode, index, 0, NULL);

with cs->status taken from the kernel. A Command Status carrying status
0 therefore reaches the callback with length 0 and param NULL, passes
the status != MGMT_STATUS_SUCCESS guard, and crashes the daemon.

Observed on a QCA9377 (13d3:3503) whose controller stops answering HCI
during audio use. The crash site was resolved from the shipped binary:

  bluetoothd[2821]: segfault at 0 ip 00005d6eb1ad1986 sp 00007ffef8e784b0 \
      error 4 in bluetoothd[a6986,5d6eb1a50000+f3000]

  a6986:  41 0f b6 45 00    movzbl 0x0(%r13),%eax     <-- cp.type = rp->type
  a698b:  0f b7 53 04       movzwl 0x4(%rbx),%edx     <-- adapter->dev_id
  a6992:  4c 8d 45 d7       lea    -0x29(%rbp),%r8    <-- &cp

Perform the same length validation before using the reply in the
no-clients branch. The check is added inside that branch rather than
hoisted above it, so that no other path changes behaviour.

The length check has been in this function since 7b897d2d3 ("core: Simplify
discovery start and stop handling", 2013-01-19). The no-clients branch that
dereferences the reply above it was added later, by 3597d1377 ("adapter: Fix
not waiting for start discovery result", 2017-08-31), so the ordering has
been wrong since then.

8b21a74f2 ("adapter: Fix crash when discovering", 2018-02-20) fixed a
different NULL dereference in this same function -- adapter->discovery_list
-- five months afterwards, and did not touch the rp dereference.

Still present in master as of 5.87-78-gc73fa2f. A search of the BlueZ issue
tracker and the web found no prior report of this specific defect, but
lore.kernel.org and patchwork.kernel.org search were both unreachable from
here, so please treat "not fixed in master" as established and "not
previously reported" as unverified.

Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 src/adapter.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/adapter.c b/src/adapter.c
--- a/src/adapter.c
+++ b/src/adapter.c
@@ -1850,6 +1850,12 @@
 		if (status != MGMT_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 			return;
 
+		if (length < sizeof(*rp)) {
+			btd_error(adapter->dev_id,
+				"Wrong size of start discovery return parameters");
+			return;
+		}
+
 		/* Stop discovering as there are no clients left */
 		cp.type = rp->type;
 		mgmt_send(adapter->mgmt, MGMT_OP_STOP_DISCOVERY,
-- 
2.43.0

